    <p class="abstract mathjax">
      <span class="search-hit">Abstract</span>:
      <span class="abstract-short has-text-grey-dark mathjax" id="2610.31354v1-abstract-short" style="display: inline;">
        ClinGuard is a model-agnostic governance framework that treats clinical coordination as patient-scoped, policy-bound <span class="search-hit mathjax">transactions</span> rather than free text. An independent sentinel layer validates and governs&hellip;
        <a class="is-size-7" style="white-space: nowrap;" onclick="document.getElementById('2610.31354v1-abstract-full').style.display = 'inline'; document.getElementById('2610.31354v1-abstract-short').style.display = 'none';">&#9661; More</a>
      </span>
      <span class="abstract-full has-text-grey-dark mathjax" id="2610.31354v1-abstract-full" style="display: none;">
        ClinGuard is a model-agnostic governance framework that treats clinical coordination as patient-scoped, policy-bound <span class="search-hit mathjax">transactions</span> rather than free text. An independent sentinel layer validates and governs <span class="search-hit mathjax">agent</span>-proposed actions, escalates when needed, and <span class="search-hit mathjax">executes</span> approved actions through limited-privilege connectors. Each <span class="search-hit mathjax">transaction</span> is linked to a tamper-evident audit record, while an outcomes monitor informs future autonomy decisions. Using MIMIC-IV-FHIR and skilled-nursing-facility placement, we distinguish retrospective demonstration from proposed prospective evaluation in this work.
        <a class="is-size-7" style="white-space: nowrap;" onclick="document.getElementById('2610.31354v1-abstract-full').style.display = 'none'; document.getElementById('2610.31354v1-abstract-short').style.display = 'inline';">&#9651; Less</a>
      </span>
    </p>
    

    <p class="is-size-7"><span class="has-text-black-bis has-text-weight-semibold">Submitted</span> 22 October, 2026; 
      <span class="has-text-black-bis has-text-weight-semibold">originally announced</span> October 2026.
      
    </p>
    
