    <p class="title is-5 mathjax">
      
        Pollard: Governed Semantic <span class="search-hit mathjax">Execution</span> Trees for Framework-Independent AI <span class="search-hit mathjax">Agent</span> Control and Replay
      
    </p>
    <p class="authors">
      <span class="has-text-black-bis has-text-weight-semibold">Authors:</span>
      
      <a href="/search/?searchtype=author&amp;query=Syed%2C+M">Muntaser Syed</a>, 
      
      <a href="/search/?searchtype=author&amp;query=Silaghi%2C+M+C">Marius C. Silaghi</a>
      
    </p>
    
    <p class="abstract mathjax">
      <span class="search-hit">Abstract</span>:
      <span class="abstract-short has-text-grey-dark mathjax" id="2610.16145v1-abstract-short" style="display: inline;">
        <span class="search-hit mathjax">Agent</span> frameworks can persist checkpoints, trace tool calls, and limit resource use, but these facilities often assign different identities to&hellip;
        <a class="is-size-7" style="white-space: nowrap;" onclick="document.getElementById('2610.16145v1-abstract-full').style.display = 'inline'; document.getElementById('2610.16145v1-abstract-short').style.display = 'none';">&#9661; More</a>
      </span>
      <span class="abstract-full has-text-grey-dark mathjax" id="2610.16145v1-abstract-full" style="display: none;">
        <span class="search-hit mathjax">Agent</span> frameworks can persist checkpoints, trace tool calls, and limit resource use, but these facilities often assign different identities to <span class="search-hit mathjax">execution</span>, governance, and replay. We present Pollard, a framework-independent runtime based on governed semantic <span class="search-hit mathjax">execution</span> trees. A step identity commits to canonical input, kind, attempt, and parent identity; the same tree records completion, refusal, resource settlement, and branch history. Strict replay returns a verified stored result without invoking the wrapped operation, while a <span class="search-hit mathjax">transactional</span> store coordinates reservations across concurrent workers. Under a signed deterministic freeze, two state-model replicas each <span class="search-hit mathjax">executed</span> the evaluation transitions without an invariant violation, retained-lease PostgreSQL groups were tested against exact limits, strict replay avoided external calls, and all semantic mutations were detected with no false alarms on the controls. A multi-pair framework matrix preserved reference behavior and verified the trees. A separate cost-capped hosted study exercised live provider paths, and every completed Pollard trial produced a verified tree. Together, the studies support the core mechanisms under explicit lease, boundary, and seal-custody assumptions.
        <a class="is-size-7" style="white-space: nowrap;" onclick="document.getElementById('2610.16145v1-abstract-full').style.display = 'none'; document.getElementById('2610.16145v1-abstract-short').style.display = 'inline';">&#9651; Less</a>
      </span>
