    <p class="title is-5 mathjax">
      
        SwingGuard: Risk-Conditioned Multi-<span class="search-hit mathjax">Agent</span> Swing Trading with Dual-Timescale Governance
      
    </p>
    <p class="authors">
      <span class="has-text-black-bis has-text-weight-semibold">Authors:</span>
      
      <a href="/search/?searchtype=author&amp;query=Su%2C+J">Junzhou Su</a>, 
      
      <a href="/search/?searchtype=author&amp;query=Luo%2C+Y">Yichen Luo</a>, 
      
      <a href="/search/?searchtype=author&amp;query=Feng%2C+Y">Yebo Feng</a>, 
      
      <a href="/search/?searchtype=author&amp;query=Li%2C+T">Teng Li</a>, 
      
      <a href="/search/?searchtype=author&amp;query=Xu%2C+J">Jiahua Xu</a>
      
    </p>
    
    <p class="abstract mathjax">
      <span class="search-hit">Abstract</span>:
      <span class="abstract-short has-text-grey-dark mathjax" id="2610.12988v1-abstract-short" style="display: inline;">
        &hellip;at the same cadence, leaving proposals unconditioned by current risk and exposure weakly governed between revisions. We propose SwingGuard, a dual-timescale, long-only multi-<span class="search-hit mathjax">agent</span> framework for risk-conditioned strategy generation. At the strategy timescale, specialized analysts synthesize point-in-time technical, sentiment, on-chain, and macroeconomic evide&hellip;
        <a class="is-size-7" style="white-space: nowrap;" onclick="document.getElementById('2610.12988v1-abstract-full').style.display = 'inline'; document.getElementById('2610.12988v1-abstract-short').style.display = 'none';">&#9661; More</a>
      </span>
      <span class="abstract-full has-text-grey-dark mathjax" id="2610.12988v1-abstract-full" style="display: none;">
        Cryptocurrency swing trading spans mismatched timescales: positions remain active while market and event risk can change within minutes. However, many predictive and large language model (LLM)-based trading systems assess risk after strategy generation or run both functions at the same cadence, leaving proposals unconditioned by current risk and exposure weakly governed between revisions. We propose SwingGuard, a dual-timescale, long-only multi-<span class="search-hit mathjax">agent</span> framework for risk-conditioned strategy generation. At the strategy timescale, specialized analysts synthesize point-in-time technical, sentiment, on-chain, and macroeconomic evidence through bullish-bearish deliberation. The resulting evidence and current risk context are then combined by a Portfolio Architect to form a target position. At the governance timescale, a five-minute Risk Controller performs conditional diagnosis, maintains persistent risk states with staged recovery, audits the proposal, and constrains <span class="search-hit mathjax">execution</span> until the next strategy revision. This design allows risk to shape the feasible strategy before proposal finalization while continuing to govern the active position afterward. Evaluations on Bitcoin (BTC) and Ether (ETH) show that SwingGuard preserves positive returns after <span class="search-hit mathjax">transaction</span> costs while maintaining shallow drawdowns and strong risk-adjusted performance on both assets. The exposure-capped joint portfolio achieves a Sharpe ratio of 2.98, compared with 2.79 for an otherwise identical Post-hoc Risk variant. Structured traces further link risk evidence and state transitions to strategy constraints and <span class="search-hit mathjax">executed</span> position changes, providing an auditable framework for asynchronous cryptocurrency swing trading. Overall, the results indicate that conditioning strategy formation on current risk, together with persistent high-frequency governance, improves risk-adjusted performance without sacrificing auditability.
        <a class="is-size-7" style="white-space: nowrap;" onclick="document.getElementById('2610.12988v1-abstract-full').style.display = 'none'; document.getElementById('2610.12988v1-abstract-short').style.display = 'inline';">&#9651; Less</a>
      </span>
    </p>
    

    <p class="is-size-7"><span class="has-text-black-bis has-text-weight-semibold">Submitted</span> 9 October, 2026; 
      <span class="has-text-black-bis has-text-weight-semibold">originally announced</span> October 2026.
      
    </p>
    
